<title>BELGIUM: EU vets Daimler-Benz /Leica buy of ADC.</title>
<headline>EU vets Daimler-Benz /Leica buy of ADC.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it was starting a routine probe into the joint acquisition of speed control systems firm ADC Automotive Distance Control Systems GmbH by a Daimler-Benz subsidiary and Leica AG of Switzerland.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the operation apparently fell under the European Union's merger regulation which bans creation or strengthening of dominant positions. The Commission has about a month to clear the deal or start a full four-month probe.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the deal, Temic Telefunken Microelectronic GmbH, an electronic components systems company which belongs to Daimler-Benz, and Leica create a joint venture in which they jointly control ADC, the Commission said. -- Brussels newsroom 32 2 2876841</p>
</text>
